{{- /*
  blog/locate-post-file — Step-1 boilerplate for blog prompts that operate on
  the post file recorded on a bead. Emits a bash block that loads the bead's
  description via `bd show ... --json`, extracts the `File: [path](path)`
  Markdown link, resolves the path, and bails with a clear error when the
  `File:` line is missing.

  The fragment reads `.Args.IssueID` from the caller's context (the epic-wide
  convention for the target-bead ID argument in the blog suite). Callers that
  invoke this fragment must pass their own dot value so `.Args.IssueID` is
  available — i.e. `{{ template "blog/shared/locate-post-file" . }}`.

  Architectural intent (mitto-98l.1): centralise the "find the post file"
  boilerplate so consumer prompts (content-review, fact-check, polish,
  publish, linkedin-post) don't each ship their own byte-drifted copy. Any
  future change to the File-line convention lands here once.
*/ -}}
Load the bead and resolve the post file recorded in its description. The
convention is a single `File: [path](path)` Markdown link that gives the
repo-relative path to the draft:

```bash
bd show {{ .Args.IssueID }} --json > /tmp/bead-{{ .Args.IssueID }}.json
file_line=$(jq -r '.[0].description' /tmp/bead-{{ .Args.IssueID }}.json \
  | grep -m1 -E '^File:[[:space:]]+\[.+\]\(.+\)' || true)
if [[ -z "$file_line" ]]; then
  echo "ERROR: bead {{ .Args.IssueID }} has no 'File: [path](path)' line in its description." >&2
  echo "Add one (e.g. via the ideation prompt) before running this stage." >&2
  exit 1
fi
# Extract the URL portion of the Markdown link and resolve it.
post_path=$(printf '%s\n' "$file_line" | sed -E 's/^File:[[:space:]]+\[[^]]+\]\(([^)]+)\).*/\1/')
post_abs=$(realpath -m -- "$post_path")
echo "post_path=$post_path"
echo "post_abs=$post_abs"
if [[ ! -f "$post_abs" ]]; then
  echo "ERROR: post file $post_abs (from File: line) does not exist on disk." >&2
  exit 1
fi
```

Downstream steps in the caller can then read `"$post_abs"` to load the draft.
